 # H7 fixture · locale trap
 
-A web plugin whose browser half locates the host session-header button by
-matching the display text `/session\s*log/i`. The host client copy has been
-fully localized (rollup R-13), so the selector silently stops matching on
-non-English locales — the injected badge disappears with no error and no
-console exception. The trap comment suggests adding a second regex. **Test
-material only — do not execute or publish** (`"private": true`).
+A web plugin that adds a small badge to the browser Session Header, beside the
+host `Session log` control. The browser half contributes through the declared
+`conversation.session.header.utilities` slot — the slot that owns that control —
+so placement, lifetime, and withdrawal follow the slot ledger rather than the
+control's localized display text. The host half registers the bundle patch
+(`cordis.patch.yml`) and the plugin lifecycle only; the browser half lives in
+`client.js`.
+
+Background: the browser half previously located the control by matching the
+display text `/session\s*log/i`. Client copy is locale-owned (rollup R-13), so
+the selector stopped matching on non-English locales and the badge disappeared
+with no error and no console exception; adding locale-specific regexes only
+moves the break to the next language. That anchoring path is retired — the slot
+contribution is the only anchor.
+
+**Test material only — do not execute or publish** (`"private": true`).
